12
01:17:42,857 --> 01:17:48,857
Vanilla Sky is a 2001 American science fiction psychological thriller film starring Tom Cruise as a
magazine publisher who begins to question reality after being disfigured in a car crash.

13
01:24:11,428 --> 01:24:17,428
Written and directed by Cameron Crowe, who also produced with Cruise and Paula Wagner, it is an English-language
remake of 1997 Spanish film Open Your Eyes, which was written by Alejandro Amenábar and Mateo Gil.

14
01:30:40,000 --> 01:30:46,000
The supporting cast includes Penélope Cruz (who reprises her role from the
original), Kurt Russell, Jason Lee, Noah Taylor, and Cameron Diaz.

15
01:37:08,571 --> 01:37:14,571
Vanilla Sky was released on December 14, 2001, grossed more than $203 million worldwide
against a production budget of $68 million, and received mixed critical reception.

16
01:43:37,142 --> 01:43:43,142
Diaz's performance was widely praised, earning her a Screen
Actors Guild and a Golden Globe Award nomination.

17
01:50:05,714 --> 01:50:11,714
The song "Vanilla Sky" by Paul McCartney was nominated for
an Academy Award for Best Original Song.

18
01:56:34,285 --> 01:56:40,285
The film later gained a cult following.

19
02:03:02,857 --> 02:03:08,857
The film explores themes of regret, jealousy,
amnesia, dreams, love of one's life.

20
02:09:31,428 --> 02:09:37,428
The tone is emotional and thought_provoking and mind_bending.
